  "order": 2,
  "title": "Block exposed backups with a disallowed URL and a disallowed file type",
  "requirement": "The application developer has told you they accidentally left backups of the SQL tables inside the application, in the /backups folder. There are other files in that folder too, but nobody can remember what they are. The application runs over HTTPS on port 443 behind the OWASP_Essentials policy, which is already in Blocking mode. Block everything in /backups, and block .sql files wherever they are in the application.",
  "intro": "Blocking the folder protects the files nobody can remember. Blocking the file type protects SQL files the developer may have left somewhere else. Do both, apply the policy, then prove it with the three test requests.",
